        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ralph Alpher, George Gamow\n- Works: Alpher–Bethe–Gamow paper\n- Roles: physics PhD student, advisor, theoretical physicist, cosmologist\n- Topics: physical cosmology\n\nFacts:\n- In physical cosmology, the Alpher–Bethe–Gamow paper was created by Ralph Alpher and his advisor George Gamow.\n- At the time of the Alpher–Bethe–Gamow paper, Ralph Alpher was a physics PhD student.\n- George Gamow was Ralph Alpher’s advisor.\n- George Gamow was born as Georgiy Antonovich Gamov on March 4, 1904, and died on August 19, 1968.\n- George Gamow was a theoretical physicist and cosmologist.",
